  "rationale": "Weight-stationary dataflow, n-blocks outer, k-blocks inner per m-block. All three A(m0,k) tiles persist in scratchpad rows 0-47 for the entire run; a single 16-row streaming slot (rows 48-63) alternates between the current B(k,n) tile and the current A(m1,k) tile. Each B(k,n) is loaded once, used by the (m0,n,k) compute (which latches it), and the (m1,n,k) compute then reuses the latched B via accumulated=true with a GARBAGE preload, so the A(m1,k) mvin may overwrite the B scratchpad copy. Per C tile the computes run k=0 (overwrite, initializing the accumulator) then k=1,2 (accumulate), giving the exact K=48 ordered reduction; both C tiles of the n-block are mvout once each after k=2. Total mvins: 3 persistent A(m0) + 9 streamed A(m1) + 9 B = 21 tiles x 256 bytes = 5376 DMA input bytes, which is a strict lower bound here: the 32-row accumulator only holds the two C tiles of one n-block, forcing n-outer processing; during an n-block all 6 A tiles and 3 B tiles are touched, at most 3 A tiles can stay resident alongside the one B streaming slot (4 tiles x 16 rows = 64 rows), so 3 A tiles load once and 3 stream in all 3 n-blocks (9 loads), plus 9 B loads. Command count 68 is minimal at this traffic: 4 configs + 21 mvins + 18 preload/compute pairs + 6 mvouts + 1 fence."
